{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "זאת תהיה תורת המצורע", :translit "zot tihyeh torat ha-metzora", :gloss "This shall be the law of the metzora"} {:he "שתי צפרים", :translit "shtei tziporim", :gloss "two birds"} {:he "כצפור נודדת מקנה כן איש נודד ממקומו", :translit "ka-tzipor nodedefet mi-ken, ken ish nodeid mi-mekomo", :gloss "Like a wandering bird from the nest, so a man wanders from his place"} {:he "בדד ישב", :translit "badad yeshev", :gloss "he shall dwell alone"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Gezeirah shavah: the bird (tzipor) of the metzora's purification parallels the wandering bird of Proverbs 27:8, since the metzora is banished and dwells alone."}], :frame {:text "The metzora must dwell alone outside the camp, as stated at Leviticus 13:46: 'he shall dwell alone; outside the camp shall be his dwelling.' Proverbs 27:8 reads: 'Like a wandering bird from the nest, so a man wanders from his place.' The Ba'al HaTurim links these by analogy: the metzora's isolation resembles a bird driven from its nest, and therefore birds are fitting for his purification.", :sources ["Leviticus 13:46" "Proverbs 27:8"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Gezeirah shavah: the bird (tzipor) of the metzora's purification parallels the wandering bird of Proverbs 27:8, since the metzora is banished and dwells alone.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:23:20.687176594Z", :model "glm-5.2"}